CIIL releases open-source speech AI for all 22 scheduled languages

The Central Institute of Indian Languages in Mysuru launched Anuvani, an open-source speech AI effort that starts with two models: one that identifies the language being spoken and one that separates speakers. Both cover all 22 scheduled languages plus Indian English and come with open weights, research papers and on-device toolkits. (Theme: new AI models and tools)



Source: The Hindu 

\[www.thehindu.com/news/national/karnataka/ciil-launches-open-source-speech-ai-ecosystem-for-indian-languages](https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/karnataka/ciil-launches-open-source-speech-ai-ecosystem-for-indian-languages/article71631788.ece)



Nvidia backs Simplismart, which helps companies run AI on fewer GPUs

Indian startup Simplismart raised a $14 million Series B led by Dallas Venture Capital, with Nvidia, Accel, Shastra VC and Micromax taking part, valuing it at about $100 million. Its software makes running AI models more efficient and, in some cases, cuts the number of GPUs needed. (Theme: AI industry and startup news)



Source: TechCrunch 

\[techcrunch.com/nvidia-backs-indian-startup-helping-companies-run-ai-models-with-fewer-gpus](https://techcrunch.com/2026/10/27/nvidia-backs-indian-startup-helping-companies-run-ai-models-with-fewer-gpus/)



Uttar Pradesh approves a robotics and AI park in Greater Noida

The UP Cabinet approved the 69.52-acre PRAGATI robotics and AI park, with shared testing, prototyping and GPU computing facilities for startups. The state projects more than 1 lakh direct and indirect jobs and Rs 2,000 crore a year in economic output at full scale; those are government estimates. (Themes: technology trends; AI policy and regulation)



Source: The Economic Times 

